<description>&lt;p&gt;Ecuador is seeing intensified state and criminal confrontations as the U.S. military assists in its first land operation against cartels, while prison gangs clashed inside a prison, killing at least 68 inmates. A journalist, Tomás Beltrán Conforme, was shot dead despite being under witness protection, and Luisa González was denied habeas corpus by an Ecuadorian court. U.S. prosecutors have charged the former president's son and four others with cocaine trafficking, linking local actors to international drug routes, and a Polish drug kingpin was arrested in Ecuador. A major Ecuadorian cocaine and weapons trafficking ring was busted in New York, and a magnitude 4.7 earthquake struck off Ecuador with no tsunami warning. The conflict recorded two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxOYXhEUmc1OTQzZmZqSU1adTk3UzFDSXBwLXQ0LVJTUkthMlpBQi0yNE40V1hLR0JuNG4wanpOZlIzTlBPMjZlN3lYTkVBbzRyQmVEOVJkcWtvWElJRHJfNE1vanRDcVFnUFlZcjJha0huX2J5clZmZU9HNTdvT2k3VmdWcmZyNHF2MUpSNloyeF9tdUxoOTlqb1pjbW1TSmdVRk1Kbnk5dlBpak96dF9WUGdtcHUtNlpTUnc?oc=5&quot;&gt;WSJ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMieEFVX3lxTE5oTE9wNnRobmkzOGkzcEJEVkRqR0VYT2N5ekxmZC00LWROMjMzUzRKak5ZNW45UmlkdlpoR1VTNnp6RmxsWDZLLThTOFp2T2pTbmN1NTI5T25NcC0zV19LRVBmQUp2eEFTSXJJdXg1blp4YmZUOTRIcA?oc=5&quot;&gt;teleSUR English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Mail&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Committee to Protect Journalists&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMibEFVX3lxTE84V19mLWVTYnpsbUZla1lMSkw0NzJvUGlvZ2d3MW1Ca2FCY1V3anZlSHluNUdXOVVQYmk2TmhuMGFGX2ZJaFdRcmFyVWVBNVJFMUJyQlVtTkhrbTd5SS1VRGhP